&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takealot Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;,&lt;/strong&gt; South Africa’s leading online retailer, is looking for a seasoned &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Director: Fulfilment &lt;/strong&gt;to join the Group’s senior technical leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you’ve been challenged before? Think again!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale&lt;/strong&gt;: 4 million happy shoppers shop online on takealot.com. Show them what you can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn&lt;/strong&gt;: We work with the best of the best, and then some. Code alongside industry leaders and upskill in record time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow&lt;/strong&gt;: Expand your career in the fast-growing Takealot Group: takealot.com and Mr D. We like to promote from within: Here’s your chance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who’s who in the tech space&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Director of Group Fulfillment&lt;/strong&gt;. Peers include the Director of Logistics, Directors of Supply Chain, Senior Operations Management, Senior QA Leadership, and Principal Engineering for Group Fulfilment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will oversee the three engineering teams responsible for the maintenance and ongoing development of Takealot Group’s fulfilment systems. This person is ultimately responsible for the systems that ensure the orchestration between our warehousing (WMS) and logistics (Routing and Courier Allocation) systems. This area is also responsible for Takealot Fulfillment Solutions (TFS) client onboarding and management. It is the ideal role for someone to sit between operations and the customer.&amp;nbsp; The role will be responsible for driving the division’s technical strategy to both innovate and manage risks spanning efficiency, scalability, security, performance, and uptime.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a technology leader who thrives in a vibrant, innovative, and collaborative environment, and who has the passion and desire to remain hands-on in a fast-paced, dynamic space. You provide leadership and direction for teams across functional areas, also developing and implementing the strategy for these functional area/s. The Engineering Director, in conjunction with the Senior Director of Group Fulfillment, is responsible for developing and sustaining a healthy engineering organization, ensuring guidance on strategic and tactical technology choices, and ensuring consistent delivery of value to both internal and external customers. You are operations-centric, a self-starter, and enjoy working in an environment that requires strong technical ability, strong ownership, and great communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission, should you choose to accept it:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable and empower the engineering managers and/or senior engineering resources in your division to drive technical innovation, vision, and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead by example: Follow best practices, promote process, foster respectful relationships with your peers and reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality and efficiency: Empower your teams to build the highest quality systems in an efficient and scalable manner.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define hiring objectives to meet business goals and support recruitment efforts by following and improving recruitment tools and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and retain multiple high-caliber engineering teams in support of your technology and product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adapt team structures to support organizational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure a culture of safety, collaboration, trust, and respect within your division and across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help your division&#39;s teams achieve their goals by removing roadblocks and interruptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and monitor Key Performance Indicators for your division&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve sources of friction and conflict across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate discussions and workshops to move teams forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote the achievements of others across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistent high-quality of deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Look for and implement opportunities for efficiency multiplication where possible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships through regular one-on-one conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain depth of oversight through skip-level one-on-one conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support career development of engineers and managers according to defined frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure teams are suitably trained to perform all job functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide coaching, guidance, and upskilling to team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage individual performance through reviews and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Address underperformance through improvement programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administration of leave and other requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onboarding for new team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview candidates for technical and cultural fit within the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Oversight&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up to date with industry trends and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present practical input for strategic technology decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and give direction to innovation in your teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain architectural oversight, building out a long-term roadmap to address risks and opportunities in your teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for the scale, reliability, efficiency, performance, security, and quality of the systems owned by your teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill up on core technologies used within engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure technical best practices and directives are adhered to in the teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relate business &amp;amp; technical objectives and requirements to actionable work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and/or delegate the agile processes within the team (standups, grooming, sprint planning, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead projects, or delegate project leadership with oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable for meeting the team&#39;s project delivery expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure teams adhere to existing engineering processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new or evolve existing processes to improve efficiency, visibility, or output for your teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a culture of operational excellence and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure adherence to best practices around incident response and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage risk actively, addressing needs around security, maintenance, scale, and reliability in your teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain the budget for systems owned by your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and maintain the budget for general team expenses (travel, social, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and support the operational efficiency of the warehouses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimise operational overheads which can slow down the development of new systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team&#39;s KPIs and operational health telemetry is up-to-date and visible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to internal engineering-related documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and/or maintain relationships with business partners and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure your teams are aware of the North Star Metric and its Input Metrics that they are influencing with the projects they deliver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evangelize and reinforce the adoption of engineering best practices across your division&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or Advanced Diploma in IT, Engineering, or any related area of study or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 10 years of experience, of which 5 years should be experience managing engineering teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing strategic technology roadmaps with customer focus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with building RESTful API web services and microservices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event-driven systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant technical experience and a proven track record of architectural ownership and understanding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A thorough understanding of computer science fundamentals, including object-oriented design, data structures, and algorithms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developing distributed, high-transactional and available systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in supply chain and/or logistics would be advantageous, but not necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The skills we need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding analysis and problem-solving abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative team working skills and expertise to achieve business goals, and build cohesiveness while valuing individual perspective and contributions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Like what you see?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind. &lt;/strong&gt;Apply today!!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Finance Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis) &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Cape Town&amp;nbsp; |&amp;nbsp; Team: Corporate FP&amp;amp;A, Takealot Group&amp;nbsp; |&amp;nbsp; Reports to: Head of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, South Africa&#39;s leading e-commerce and marketplace, is looking for a highly talented Finance Analyst to own the Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis pillar of our Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate FP&amp;amp;A is on a journey from operational reporting to strategic value creation. This role sits at the heart of that shift: you will own the Group&#39;s standardised internal reporting infrastructure and month-end process, and lead the automation agenda that frees the wider team to focus on strategic analysis, planning and CFO/CEO support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the accountable owner of a pillar, not a contributor to it. You will set the standard for reporting accuracy and timeliness across all business units (Retail, Marketplace, Trade Optimisation, CatOps and Marketing, MrD, TFS), drive the automation of month-end and recurring reporting, and develop a Junior Finance Analyst within the pillar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar ownership: reporting infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Group&#39;s standardised reporting suite across all BUs, ensuring a single, consistent version of the truth for Exco, divisional leadership and the Board pack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design, maintenance and governance of finance Looker reporting, including dashboards relied on by Accounts Payable, FinOps and Customer &amp;amp; Insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain reporting standards, data definitions and controls that safeguard the accuracy, completeness and validity of management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month-end &amp;amp; operational excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the FP&amp;amp;A month-end process end to end: timetable, deliverables, reconciliations to the ledger and management accounts, and quality review before release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify root causes of reporting errors and late deliverables, and implement permanent fixes rather than manual workarounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document end-to-end processes, interdependencies and system touchpoints (e.g. TM1, Looker) and keep them current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; process redesign&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the pillar&#39;s automation roadmap: prioritise opportunities by hours saved and risk reduced, then deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and redesign processes using SQL, Looker, Excel/Gsheets(AppsScripts) and AI tools to remove manual, high-volume work from the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Finance&#39;s lead representative on reporting and data projects, partnering with BI, IT, Tech and Product to specify requirements, get the right data points into the correct models/cubes, test outputs and sign off delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People &amp;amp; stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise, coach and quality-review the work of the Junior Finance Analyst in the pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with BU finance partners and operational teams, and communicate clearly with senior stakeholders on reporting changes, issues and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cover and support to the Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting and Strategic Analysis &amp;amp; Insights pillars during peak cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Success Is Measured:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Report accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; reduction in post-release corrections and reconciling differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Timeliness: &lt;/strong&gt;month-end and recurring reports delivered on or ahead of the agreed timetable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation rate:&lt;/strong&gt; share of recurring reporting and month-end tasks automated; analyst hours released to strategic work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team development&lt;/strong&gt;: growth and output quality of the Junior Finance Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner&#39;s mindset: takes full accountability for a pillar&#39;s outcomes, not just its tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinker who understands how data flows through the business and where it breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail combined with the judgement to know what matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder and doer: designs the solution and executes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise written and verbal communicator, confident with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative partner to BI, Tech and Product; able to translate finance needs into technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, changing environment and juggles competing priorities calmly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach who raises the capability of those around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCom (Hons) or equivalent in Finance/Accounting; CA(SA), CIMA or CFA (completed or in progress) advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years&#39; relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, management reporting or a finance/BI role, including ownership of a month-end or reporting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of delivering reporting automation or process redesign with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of accounting, management accounts and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel and working SQL skills; experience building in Looker or a similar BI tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with TM1, Sage and Board beneficial; exposure to Python or AI/automation tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, retail, marketplace or tech highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising or mentoring junior analysts preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it&#39;s all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Finance Analyst (Strategic Analysis &amp;amp; Insights) &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to: Head of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, South Africa&#39;s leading e-commerce and marketplace, is looking for a highly talented Finance Analyst to own the Strategic Analysis &amp;amp; Insights pillar of our Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate FP&amp;amp;A is on a journey from operational reporting to strategic value creation. This role sits at the heart of that shift: you will own the Group&#39;s strategic analysis capability — turning business questions into actionable insights, deep-diving profitability across categories, suppliers and customers, and providing the analytical foundation for CFO, CEO and Board decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the accountable owner of a pillar, not a contributor to it. You will set the standard for analytical depth and insight quality across all business units, drive the automation of recurring analysis, and mentor junior analysts across the FP&amp;amp;A team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar ownership: strategic analysis &amp;amp; insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Group&#39;s strategic analysis agenda across all BUs, ensuring Exco, divisional leadership and the Board receive actionable, decision-grade insights — not data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and continually refine the P&amp;amp;L logic to reflect current business operations, delivering the most accurate profitability analysis at category, supplier, customer and product level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn business questions into structured analysis: understand the business and the data behind it, frame the right question, and deliver a recommendation — not a chart.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain analytical standards, data definitions and governance that safeguard the validity and consistency of insights across BUs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profitability and performance analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead deep-dive profitability analysis across all BUs: unit economics, contribution margin drivers, AOV, take rate, GMV, and cost-to-serve by channel, category and customer segment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing optimisation, revenue opportunity and lost-opportunity analysis that Retail and Marketplace teams can act on to improve metrics and increase sales and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform analyses to provide insights into areas of risk and opportunity to influence pricing strategies and commercial decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce monthly management insights comparing business performance to plans, unpacking variances with root-cause clarity, not just variance descriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and perform complex, multi-variable analyses applying appropriate statistical methodologies to resolve operational and business concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic projects and CFO/CEO support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and deliver cross-BU strategic projects: MrD finance analytics, TFS growth analysis, marketplace profitability, new-business-case modelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct analytical support to the CFO and CEO on capital allocation, investment cases, and strategic decisions — own the numbers behind the narrative.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist and be actively involved in the annual Takealot Group budgeting and forecasting process, providing the analytical backbone for assumptions and challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consider multiple scenarios, points of view and potential outcomes to recommend actions based on analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; process redesign&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the pillar&#39;s automation roadmap: prioritise analytical processes by hours saved and insight quality gained, then deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and redesign analytical workflows using SQL, Looker, Excel/Gsheets(AppsScript) and AI tools to remove manual, high-volume work and free the team for strategic analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Finance&#39;s lead representative on analytical and data projects, partnering with BI, IT, Tech and Product to specify requirements, get the right data points into the correct models, test outputs and sign off delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People &amp;amp; stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with BU finance partners, operational teams and senior stakeholders, and communicate insights with clarity and commercial judgement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and develop junior analysts across the FP&amp;amp;A team, raising analytical capability and output quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cover and support to the Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis and Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting pillars during peak cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Success Is Measured:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insight quality: analysis that drives decisions, not just describes results; reduction in &quot;so what?&quot; follow-ups from Exco.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business impact: measurable outcomes from recommended actions — revenue captured, cost avoided, margin improved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Timeliness: strategic analysis and project deliverables completed on or ahead of agreed deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation rate: share of recurring analytical tasks automated; analyst hours released to higher-value work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team development: growth and analytical capability of mentored analysts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner&#39;s mindset: takes full accountability for a pillar&#39;s outcomes, not just its tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinker who understands how data flows through the business and where it breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail combined with the judgement to know what matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder and doer: designs the solution and executes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise written and verbal communicator, confident with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative partner to BI, Tech and Product; able to translate finance needs into technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, changing environment and juggles competing priorities calmly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach who raises the capability of those around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCom (Hons) or equivalent in Finance/Accounting; CA(SA), CIMA or CFA (completed or in progress) advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years&#39; relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, strategic analysis, management reporting or a finance/BI role, including ownership of an analytical or reporting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of delivering analytical automation or process redesign with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of accounting, management accounts, financial reporting and P&amp;amp;L logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel and working SQL skills; experience building in Looker or a similar BI tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with TM1, Sage and Board beneficial; exposure to Python or AI/automation tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, retail, marketplace or tech highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising or mentoring junior analysts preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it&#39;s all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a methodical, analytical graduate to join us on a 12-month development programme. You&#39;ll work across our operations, talking to real teams to understand how they work, then translate that into clear, documented processes that help everyone do their job better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is your chance to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map how key business processes work end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct interviews and walkthroughs with frontline teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear, standardised documentation that everyone can follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, workarounds, and areas for improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain deep exposure to how a large-scale e-commerce operation works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Industrial Engineering, Operations, or related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Methodical, process-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with process mapping tools (Visio, Lucidchart, &lt;a href=&quot;http://draw.io&quot;&gt;io&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-driven with strong ownership of your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic SQL or data literacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of process notation (BPMN, swimlane diagrams)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;E-commerce or logistics operations experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Develop&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over 12 months, you&#39;ll develop skills in process documentation, stakeholder engagement, technical communication, and operations management. You&#39;ll work with teams across our entire business and have the chance to create documentation that powers training, automation, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ready to Join?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re a methodical graduate who enjoys working with people, documenting processes, and making a real impact on how a large operation runs, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Life @ Takealot Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No doors:&lt;/strong&gt; Open, collaborative culture — work with the best&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid working:&lt;/strong&gt; Balance office and remote work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global learning:&lt;/strong&gt; Access to platforms like Udacity, Coursera, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tech stack for days:&lt;/strong&gt; Python, Scala, Kotlin, Google Cloud, Kafka, Kubernetes, ML tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good times:&lt;/strong&gt; Social events, team activities, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff discount:&lt;/strong&gt; Millions of products at your fingertips&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Birthday leave:&lt;/strong&gt; Because cake matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to &lt;strong&gt;build the future of AI in a real business environment&lt;/strong&gt;, this is your opportunity. &lt;span class=&quot;_textBold_cax8s_148&quot;&gt;To apply, simply submit your CV and academic transcripts. Let’s see what you’ve got!&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
