&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Operations Manager: Social Impact&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Takealot Group Advertising team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard working people to join us.&amp;nbsp; We offer market related benefits, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the operationalisation and delivery management of Takealot Group’s social-impact portfolio under the strategic direction of the Socio-Economic Development Manager, across Skills Development, Enterprise Development and Socio-Economic Development. Translate approved programme strategies, funding proposals and partnership agreements with SETAs, development-finance institutions and government agencies into executable plans, compliant administration, controlled budgets, effective partner delivery, accurate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;beneficiary records and audit-ready evidence. Build a leveraged funding model that protects theGroup’s B-BBEE recognition, converts approved opportunities into contracted and collected funding, recovers permissible programme-management costs and reduces the net cost of programme delivery&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Programme operationalisation and delivery&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate approved programme strategies, memoranda of understanding and funding agreements into project charters, integrated workplans, budgets, responsibility matrices,milestones and reporting calendars.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct implementation-readiness reviews and confirm that beneficiary criteria, delivery partners, systems, data, budgets, safeguards and evidence requirements are in place before launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the integrated portfolio plan and action, decision, issue, risk and dependency registers;coordinate operating reviews, corrective action, recovery plans and formal change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage operational close-out, final reconciliations, evidence collation, lessons learned and handover into sustainable business processes where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Funding proposal support and partner administration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Socio-Economic Development Manager in developing funding proposals by preparing implementation models, costed budgets, administration-fee structures, delivery plans, compliance requirements, evidence frameworks and partner arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an operational view of relevant SETA, government and development-finance opportunities, funding windows, eligibility requirements and submission deadlines, aligned to agreed portfolio priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate applications, statutory documentation, due diligence, contracting, conditions precedent, portal submissions and responses to funder queries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track funding applied for, approved, contracted, claimed, disbursed, committed, spent and remaining, and ensure reports, claims, amendments and close-out submissions are accurate and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;SETA and skills-development administration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the operational requirements of discretionary grants, strategic partnerships and workplace-based learning programmes, including WSP and ATR inputs where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify learner eligibility, agreements, registrations, files, attendance, stipend schedules, assessments, completion and certification, together with provider accreditation and workplace approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reconcile funded, registered, active, completed, certified and exited learners; manage withdrawals, replacements, remediation and other programme exceptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate SETA monitoring visits, verification exercises, information requests and audits, maintaining complete and accessible learner evidence records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Enterprise development and DFI operations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalise enterprise-development and funding partnerships approved by the Socio Economic Development Manager, translating NEF, SEDFA and other funder requirements into practical screening, application-readiness and due-diligence processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the enterprise funding pipeline and coordinate the collection and verification of registration, ownership, tax, financial, governance and compliance information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track applications through assessment, contracting,fulfilment of conditions, disbursement and post- investment monitoring, coordinating specialist support where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate reporting on enterprises screened, referred, submitted, approved, declined, contracted and funded, together with agreed business and socio- economic outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Financial control, funding leverage and commercial value&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain programme budgets, eligible-cost mappings, partner funding, Takealot contributions, co-funding and in-kind contributions, with monthly budget-versus-actual reconciliations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate invoices, payment packs, milestones and claims against approved budgets and delivery evidence;track commitments, accruals, recoveries, disbursements and unspent funds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build permissible programme-administration, project-management and implementation costs into funding proposals and agreements so that funded portfolios contribute to their own operating capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quantify and report grant recoveries, programme cost offsets, role cost coverage, funding leverage and avoided leakage while protecting qualifying B-BBEE expenditure and preventing double counting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Data, governance, partner performance and improvement&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain authoritative learner, beneficiary and enterprise records with clear data standards, verification controls, consent management and POPIA compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce portfolio dashboards, partner reports and decision-ready insights for the Socio Economic Development Manager, and provide validated data and evidence for Group sustainability and impact reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage implementation partners through clear deliverables, service levels, scorecards, site reviews and remediation; validate performance before recommending milestone approval or payment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardise operating procedures, templates and funder playbooks; automate recurring workflows and build organisational knowledge of SETA and government funding systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Funding conversion and net financial contribution&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert approved funding opportunities into contracted, claimed and collected funding that complements or replaces approved Takealot programme expenditure, while maintaining the Group contribution required to achieve targeted B-BBEE outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recover approved administration and project-management fees and demonstrate a role cost coverage ratio of at least 1.0x once the funded portfolio reaches operating scale, with a positive net financial contribution thereafter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Programme delivery and funding administration&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver at least 90% of controllable programme milestones on time or under an approved recovery plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Submit all controllable applications, claims and partner reports by deadline, with a high first time acceptance rate and no avoidable loss of approved funding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Financial control and B-BBEE assurance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete monthly programme and funding reconciliations within the agreed timetable and ensure all claims and payment recommendations are supported by valid evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear separation between external funding and Takealot qualifying contributions, with zero avoidable double counting, clawbacks or disallowed expenditure attributable to programme administration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Data, compliance and partner performance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain at least 98% completeness across required beneficiary, learner and enterprise records and fulfil evidence requests within agreed turnaround times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve sustained service-provider compliance through scorecards, documented remediation and timely escalation, with no material or repeated administrative audit findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Management and executive reporting&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide the Socio-Economic Development Manager with a concise, decision-ready view of the funding pipeline, financial contribution, delivery performance, beneficiary reach, partner performance, risks and decisions required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain evidence-based case studies and lessons that strengthen future programme design, funding proposals, partner engagements and the scalability of the Group social-impact portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Qualification:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A relevant bachelors in degree in BusinessAdministration, Commerce, Finance, Public Administration, Project Management, Development Studies, Development Finance, Skills Development, Monitoring and Evaluation or a related discipline. A relevant postgraduate or recognised project- management qualification is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years relevant experience in programme operations, funded-project delivery, grants, skills development, enterprise development or development-finance administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least four years&amp;amp;#39; direct experience administering SETA-, government- or development-finance-funded programmes, including end-to-end SETA programme administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex, multi-partner programmes and multi-million-rand budgets across applications, due diligence, contracting, claims, disbursement, reporting, audit and close out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing learner, beneficiary or enterprise records at scale and coordinating training providers, implementing partners or business-development service providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational excellence; programme and project management; funding and compliance acumen; financial judgement; systems thinking; commercial and risk awareness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional influence, stakeholder management, constructive assertiveness, structured problem solving and the ability to work effectively across corporate and government systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrity, attention to detail, evidence orientation, accountability for delivery and the confidence to escalate risks and challenge incomplete work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

