&lt;p&gt;Takealot.com, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly talented Principal Technical Program Manager to join the Engineering &amp;amp; Product team based in Cape Town, South Africa.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you&#39;ve been challenged before? Think again!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale: &lt;/strong&gt;4 million happy shoppers shop online on takealot.com. Show them what you can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn: &lt;/strong&gt;We work with the best of the best, and then some. Code alongside industry leaders and up-skill in record time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow: &lt;/strong&gt;Expand your career in the fast-growing Takealot Group: takealot.com, Mr D, and TFS. We like to promote from within: Here&#39;s your chance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Principal Technical Program Manager owns the integrated delivery plan and cross-programme view across Takealot Group&#39;s largest parallel engineering programmes. These multi-team initiatives, spanning app integrations, core platform migrations, and logistics re-architecture, cross numerous teams, systems, and business units while drawing on the same shared pool of senior engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role involves building bottom-up delivery plans grounded in real scope and real team throughput, identifying critical paths, and escalating cross-programme trade-offs early to the right decision-makers with clear options and the cost of delay for each. While each individual programme retains its own delivery lead for day-to-day execution, the Principal Technical Program Manager plays a pivotal role in orchestrating cross-programme alignment, capacity visibility, and executive decision-making across the Group Engineering function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrated Programme Planning &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end integrated delivery plan across major parallel engineering programmes, and answer for committed delivery dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build delivery plans bottom-up from actual Jira scope and real team throughput, challenging any estimate that cannot be traced to either.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify critical paths and re-sequence work where necessary to shorten delivery timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dependency &amp;amp; Capacity Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map dependencies across internal teams, system components, and external parties (including app store reviews, contractors, and vendors), assigning a clear owner and need-by date to every dependency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a single, consolidated view of shared senior engineering capacity across programmes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate capacity conflicts and resource trade-offs early to the Group CTO and relevant decision forums, backed by clear options and the quantified cost of delay for each.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, Cadence &amp;amp; Executive Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the programme governance rhythm, including weekly delivery reviews and consolidated risk and issue registers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide structured programme inputs to steering committees, executive gates, and weekly/monthly business reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
