&lt;p&gt;Takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Programme Lead: Marketplace &amp;amp; SMME Development &lt;/strong&gt;join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us.  We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To lead the design, delivery and scaling of the Takealot Group’s marketplace-facing SMME and enterprise-development programmes — building sustainable entrepreneurs and expanding market access for township and small businesses across the Takealot and Mr D platforms and to deliver the marketplace portfolio’s contribution to the Group’s socio-economic development and lives-impacted commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programme strategy &amp;amp;amp; design. Design scaffolded, phased seller- and enterprise development programmes (readiness → growth → sustain → scale) grounded in experiential learning and the realities of the South African SMME landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programme delivery &amp;amp;amp; scaling. Own end-to-end delivery across the marketplace portfolio - Seller Growth (Marketplace Localisation), Mr D Mzantsi Trailblazers, the Beauty Programme,iNkundla Rural Entrepreneurship, the Innovation Challenge and YES for Marketplace — driving seller activation, growth, retention and survival outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder &amp;amp;amp; partner management. Manage delivery partners and training providers, internal Marketplace and Mr D business units, and external partners including Services SETA, DHET and funders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team leadership. Lead, coach and develop the programme coordinators; set objectives, manage performance and build delivery capability as the team scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitoring, evaluation &amp;amp;amp; reporting. Work with the M&amp;amp;amp;Efunction to define measurement, ensure evidence-grade reporting, and report programme performance to leadership, Services SETA and Prosus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Budget &amp;amp;amp; funding. Manage programme budgets and grant-funded delivery, support funding proposals, and ensure grant compliance within the Services SETA–DHET partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Qualification:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant bachelor’s degree (Business, Economics, Development Studies, Commerce or related); a postgraduate qualification is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years’ relevant experience, including demonstrable SMME / enterprise-development experience AND experience in marketplace, e-commerce or retail environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 3 years leading programmes and teams, with a track record of scaling development programmes and managing multi-stakeholder partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of grant-funded programme delivery and B-BBEE Enterprise &amp;amp;amp; Supplier Development / Socio- Economic Development is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of SMME / enterprise development and the South African entrepreneurship landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of marketplace and e-commerce dynamics —seller onboarding, seller economics and market access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programme design and management; monitoring and evaluation; financial and budget management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder engagement, people leadership, strategic and analytical thinking, and a strong results orientation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, its all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to Employ an &lt;strong&gt;Extra Ordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; who:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is respectful but forthright&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is an expert at doing, who can not only design but also execute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is analytical, able to use data to make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is competitive, self-directed and strive to be the BEST (GREAT requires a lot of work and does not only happen during business hours)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;passionate about the potential of e-commerce&lt;/strong&gt; and delivering a &lt;strong&gt;world-class customer experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;entrepreneurial&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;thrives under change&lt;/strong&gt; and accepts it is a constant and always &lt;strong&gt;looks for solutions&lt;/strong&gt; to do something better and faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is business SMART. Able to think about problems from a business perspective using technical and product input;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is curious and challenge the status quo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is innovative and enjoys iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is collaborative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;will be at the cutting edge of developing new concepts for takealot.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;thinks like an owner&lt;/strong&gt; of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;SMART, has INTEGRITY&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;is HARD WORKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; so come and join us!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;Takealot.com&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programme Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our team in &lt;strong&gt;Cape Town&lt;/strong&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard- working people to join us. We offer market related benefits, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role reports to the: &lt;/strong&gt;CEO, Takealot.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role&lt;/strong&gt;: The Program Manager helps the Takealot.com leadership team&amp;nbsp;perform better: they help bring structure to how the team works,&amp;nbsp;track commitments, and surface problems in the numbers early, so&lt;br&gt;the CEO and leaders can act on them. The role gives the CEO more&amp;nbsp;time for decisions, customers and people by taking on the&amp;nbsp;coordination work that sits between teams. This person owns the&amp;nbsp;shared operating rhythm across the leadership team and its direct&amp;nbsp;reports, with a direct line of sight to the company scoreboard (GMV&amp;nbsp;growth, Retail Media revenue, premium delivery share).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the existing leadership operating rhythm (weekly&amp;nbsp;leadership meeting, monthly business reviews, quarterly planning&amp;nbsp;and goal setting) and help improve it over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare agendas, pre-reads and decision logs so meetings end with clear owners, dates and decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep one shared view of team priorities, initiatives and commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional work between Retail, Marketplace, Retail Media, Marketing and Logistics and Returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the leadership team for key reviews and forums with briefs and open-item status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track every leadership commitment and strategic initiative against agreed milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the progress view for the CEO’s reviews; flag slippage early with the facts and a clear ask (decision, resource or escalation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep commitment status visible to the leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up on actions from leadership meetings and close the loop until each one is formally done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply one tracker and one standard to every leader’s commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the OPCO forum, that brings all key functions of the company together (Customer service, Logistics, Returns etc.) for the customer and surfaces running issues and also helps build strategic projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyse weekly performance data (GMV, Retail Media, delivery, stock loss, customer and seller metrics etc.) against plan and last year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot variances that matter, separate noise from real risk, and check known decisions before raising an alarm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn each flag into a short, sourced note: what moved, by how much, likely cause, owner, and recommended next step.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Data and Finance teams to help strengthen reporting for overall takealot.com business health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own 1–2 strategic projects a quarter end to end: problem framing, analysis, options, recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build senior-level presentations for Exco, Group forums and town halls, including strategy narratives and season plans (e.g. Black Friday).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run deep dives on questions the leadership team needs answered fast, typically in 1–2 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;What are you expected to deliver&amp;nbsp;within the scope of&amp;nbsp;your role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;30 days&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knows every leader, initiative and metric owner. Has mapped&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;current meetings, trackers and reports, and suggested&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;improvements to the operating rhythm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;90 days&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agreed improvements to the rhythm in place. One commitment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;tracker in use by all leaders. A weekly data-flag note goes to the&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;leadership team. First strategic project or presentation Delivered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;180 days&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitments are tracked consistently and delivered on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leaders get the information they need without having to ask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leaders see the role as a trusted partner who helps them deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns at least one recurring leadership deliverable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, retail, or marketplaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQL or similar skills to pull and analyse your own data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a Chief of Staff, strategy, or PMO role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI tools to automate tracking and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An owner, not a messenger—follows through without being asked and closes loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frank and calm—raises bad news early and directly, with facts and a proposed fix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trusted with confidential information and discreet when handling people, financial, and Board matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A simplifier who removes meetings, reports, and steps rather than adding them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable switching between a Board-level narrative and a line-item variance in the same day.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lives Takealot’s values: obsess about customers, achieve more together, do the extraordinary, and deliver results fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a 2–3-year role with strong exposure to the full business and a natural springboard into a general management or senior commercial role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Degree in business, engineering, economics or a quantitative field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;5–8 years in management consulting, strategy and operations, program management, or commercial/analytics roles; a background in any of these is welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Track record of running cross-functional programs with senior stakeholders and no formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong with numbers: comfortable in Excel/Google Sheets and BI tools (Looker or similar); can read a P&amp;amp;L and a KPI dashboard and find the story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Excellent structured writing and presentation skills; can turn a messy problem into a clear 5-slide story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, South Africa’s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly talented&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Promotions and Merchandising Manager - Cross Border &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you’ve been challenged before? Think again!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Over 4 million happy shoppers shop online on takealot.com and 2.7 million on Mr D. Show them what you can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn:&lt;/strong&gt; We work with the best of the best. Work alongside leaders and upskill in record time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow:&lt;/strong&gt; Expand your career in the fast-growing Takealot Group: Takealot.com and Mr D. We like to promote from within: Here&#39;s your chance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Promotions and Merchandising Manager is responsible for developing and executing a clear merchandising strategy for the Cross Border business unit. The role drives promotional share of GMV and promotional conversion rate optimisation, ensuring that Cross Border deals are sourced, vetted, positioned, and promoted effectively across the Takealot platform. This is a hands-on, commercially driven role that sits at the intersection of sales, marketing, and trade optimisation bridging the gap between seller deal supply and customer- facing merchandising to unlock GMV growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Merchandising Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and own the Cross Border merchandising strategy and promotional calendar, aligned to seasonal peaks, category priorities, and business unit GMV targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track promotional share of GMV as a core performance metric, with clear targets and improvement plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse promotional conversion rates across deal types, categories, and merchandising placements; identify and action opportunities to improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use platform data (pageviews, conversion, AISP, search trends, lead-time share) to inform deal selection and merchandising positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Sourcing &amp;amp; Vetting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source deals from Cross Border sellers and aggregator partners, building a pipeline of promotional inventory ahead of seasonal and campaign windows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vet and qualify deals for margin contribution, product quality, compliance, and customer appeal before inclusion in promotions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate promotional terms pricing, rebates, cash-back, sell-through bonuses within the established promotional framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a deal pipeline and tracking system that provides visibility on upcoming promotions, deal quality, and expected GMV contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Positioning and Placement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Position vetted deals into relevant existing promotions and merchandising pages across the Takealot platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Cross Border products are represented in category-specific and seasonal promotional pages, themed campaigns, and front-store placements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise deal visibility through effective titling, imagery, categorisation, and page positioning.F&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor deal performance post-launch and adjust placement and promotion mechanics based on results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the marketing team to create bespoke promotions and merchandising solutions tailored to&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross Border product characteristics (lead-time, unbranded assortment, value positioning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the trade optimisation team to develop and test merchandising formats, landing pages, and promotional mechanics that drive conversion for Cross&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Border Products.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the sales team to identify merchandising opportunities within seller and aggregator portfolios that support GMV growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with operations on promotional stock readiness, lead-time communication, and customer expectations for cross-border fulfilment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the sales team in growing GMV through merchandising-led initiatives — deal curation, promotional calendar alignment, and category-level campaign planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide data and insights to the sales team on promotional performance, deal quality, and merchandising opportunities within their portfolios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with BDAs to identify high-potential products and sellers for promotional inclusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Qualification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (Business, Marketing, Commerce, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–3 years experience in a sales and marketing-related role and/or ecommerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capability — comfortable working with data, dashboards, and performance metrics to drive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-savvy — proficient in spreadsheet analysis, comfortable with platform analytics tools, and able to translate data into merchandising actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work independently and take ownership of initiatives end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills — able to work effectively across sales, marketing, and operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in ecommerce (marketplace, retail, or platform environment).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with promotional planning, deal curation, or merchandising in a consumer-facing business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Cross Border trade dynamics — lead-time fulfilment, international sellers, and unbranded/value assortments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to aggregator or multi-seller deal sourcing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge &amp;amp; Abilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial acumen — understands margin, pricing mechanics, and the levers that drive GMV. Analytical thinking — uses data to identify trends, test hypotheses, and make evidence-based decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership and initiative — drives outcomes without needing constant direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management — builds productive relationships across functions and with external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail — ensures deal quality, compliance, and positioning are consistently high.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptability — thrives in a fast-paced, evolving business unit environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Let’s talk about life @ Takealot Group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The power is in your hands&lt;/strong&gt;: We offer a market-related Total Remuneration Package that allows full flexibility according to your needs. Go on, be the master of your own destiny.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No doors&lt;/strong&gt;: We aren’t fans of stuffy offices or siloed work environments. See someone you like? High five, collab, and make something great.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote working&lt;/strong&gt;: Love water cooler chats &lt;em&gt;and &lt;/em&gt;working from home? Takealot.com offers a hybrid working model for the best of both worlds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship programme&lt;/strong&gt;: We aren’t kidding when we say the people with the best people win. Now’s your chance to be one of the best by learning from the best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Naspers Tech Community&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;&amp;amp; Online Learning&lt;/strong&gt;: Share ideas and grow with global industry leaders who are all just a Slack message away. Love to learn? Up-skill with free access to courses on MyAcademy, Udacity, Coursera, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Good times&lt;/strong&gt;: Get to know the other extraordinary minds at takealot.com during regular social events and out-of-office activities (think hikes, think mini-golf, think good times).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Staff discount&lt;/strong&gt;. Millions of products across 28 departments. What more could you ask for?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Birthday leave:&lt;/strong&gt; Cake Day all the way. Enjoy your day off - you deserve it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Right tools, right job&lt;/strong&gt;: Mac or Windows, two monitors or one. Whatever your preference, you’ll work on the latest tech of the latest tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help when you need it most&lt;/strong&gt;: Confidential counselling, legal support and financial guidance, for free, anytime, anywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Free parking: &lt;/strong&gt;No more 5km fun runs to your desk (unless you want to).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Like what you see?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above, you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind. &lt;/strong&gt;Apply today!!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mr D, &lt;/strong&gt;a division of the Takealot Group, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Senior&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Machine Learning Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team. We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you’ve been challenged before? Think again!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale&lt;/strong&gt;: Millions of happy shoppers use Mr D. Show them what you can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn&lt;/strong&gt;: We work with the best of the best, and then some. Work alongside industry leaders and up-skill in record time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow&lt;/strong&gt;: Expand your career in the fast-growing Takealot Group: &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, Mr D &amp;amp; Takealot Fulfilment Solutions. We like to promote from within: Here’s your chance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position reports to the Machine Learning Engineering Manager.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Machine Learning Engineer, your expertise directly translates into the &lt;strong&gt;development of robust machine learning models in the e-commerce domain&lt;/strong&gt;. You come from a development background with an emphasis on &lt;strong&gt;applied&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;machine learning&lt;/strong&gt;. You will have the opportunity to implement best practices to improve the existing machine learning models and participate in the development of new ones.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to contribute to a growing and dynamic team of machine learning engineers working on Mr D’s&amp;nbsp; ambitious development roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
